;; Public bots the Marketplace offers for installation.
;;
;; Hand-written, deliberately small. `src/cloud/itonami/app/public_bot_catalog.cljk`
;; validates this shape and refuses to start on drift, so an entry added here
;; without the fields the installer needs fails loudly rather than rendering a
;; half-card.
;;
;; What an entry is: a colleague-with-a-role another organization has decided
;; to offer (ADR-0097: Marketplace Bot = "a colleague with a role and
;; permissions"). Installing one creates a fresh Bot in the installer's own
;; organization via the same `bots/create!` path the "new Bot" form uses. It
;; never copies the original's conversation history, credentials, wallets or
;; accounts; the declared default capabilities below are recorded as the
;; catalog's suggestion and stay inert unless the human installer's session
;; approves them (ADR-0088: default grants stay inert).
;;
;; `:author` is the operating organization, `:entry-url` is where its published
;; work can be seen, `:install {:defaults ...}` is what a fresh install would
;; carry. `:installed-surface` names the app surface (aozora/isekai) the bot
;; publishes to — displayed on the card, not granted by it.
{:schema "cloud.itonami.app.public-bot-catalog.v1"
 :bots
 [{:id "mangaka"
   :name "mangaka (漫画家)"
   :avatar "✒"
   :role "漫画制作"
